From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:07:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Boost colours paint the page from two colours, as
 Arc's

The pad's colours no longer turn the whole page with a filter. The page is
painted as CSS from a palette of the two picked colours: neutral
backgrounds take a tint of the main colour, big coloured blocks (headers,
heroes, gradients) turn to it, buttons, badges and links to the second
one. Lightness stays, so light sites stay light and dark ones dark; text
is then made readable on what's under it (WCAG AA: 4.5:1, 3:1 for large
text). Pictures and video are not touched. Pages that change are painted
again, at most once a second; No colour or turning the boost off takes it
all back at once.

The small knob on the pad is the second colour now: drag it round to pick
the hue of buttons and links (until then it follows the main one). Saved
as tint2 (agents can set it too).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
